1
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,020
Somehow, it'll work out.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

3
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:11,900
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.

5
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,240
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

6
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,480
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

7
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,860
Lemon, what's wrong? Why that face?

9
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,240
Hey, Kankichi!

10
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:02,480
My family's a handful,
and summer vacation is almost over.

11
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,320
You aren't taking us anywhere, are you?

12
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,620
Is that all?

13
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,320
It's not "that." Take a look at this.

14
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:14,340
Picture diaries. I was made to draw
those all the time when I was a kid.

15
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,360
How nostalgic. Let's see, let's see.

16
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:23,040
Went to the pool. It was fun.

17
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:26,900
Took Mikan for a walk. It was hot.

18
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:30,020
"Went to the pool, it was fun,"

19
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:32,080
The rest are all the same, aren't they?

20
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,800
Only one is different!

21
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,600
What's this?

22
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:40,260
My relative Kankichi
came to help at the shop.

23
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,360
I got drunk and did a naked
dance with the customers.

24
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,660
It was embarrassing.

25
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:46,820
I shouldn't write things like this.

26
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,800
It can't be helped, can it?

27
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:52,640
since we didn't get taken
anywhere during summer vacation.

28
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,480
Why don't you take Gepard out?

29
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,040
Well, that's true.

30
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:00,440
Kankichi, take us somewhere, won't you?

31
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,400
Me?

32
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,860
Yes, Kankichi.

33
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:06,270
I could take you, I suppose,

34
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,840
but I'd need some money up front, you know.

35
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,420
You're family,
and you have no goodwill at all?

36
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,037
In that case, I can't do it.

37
00:03:14,087 --> 00:03:16,720
It's more helpful for me to
work my part-time job here.

38
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:17,720
Granny.

39
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:22,920
Fine, fine. Honestly, I'll pay you for your
part-time wages and your transportation costs too.

40
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,860
Yes! Lemon, be happy.

41
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,220
That's great, isn't it?

42
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,680
As usual, you're not cute at all.

43
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,520
So where are we going, Lemon?
Mountains or sea?

44
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:38,440
That's right, Lemon's totally
hooked on Hayate no Oen these days.

45
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,220
Hayate no Oen.

46
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,580
She's the female ninja from
the new Mito Kōmon series.

47
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,300
The old Crimson Ogin?

48
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,760
Yes, ninjas are strong and cool, you know.

49
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:52,520
Kankichi, I want to meet a real ninja.

50
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,000
A real ninja

51
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,840
Then I know someone.

52
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,140
Really, Kankichi?

53
00:03:59,140 --> 00:03:59,584
Yeah,

54
00:03:59,634 --> 00:04:04,740
Old man Volvo runs a museum in
Kagoshima that doubles as a ninja house.

55
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,400
That sounds fun. I think I'll go too.

56
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:10,810
Kyushu They have great
hot springs there too,

57
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,320
so I think I'll go too.

58
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:15,900
Let's go, let's go! The more people on a trip,
the more fun it is.

59
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,720
Lemon, you're going to become a kunoichi.

60
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,520
It's like a scene from a period drama.

61
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,220
There aren't any telephone poles!

62
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:38,780
There really is a ninja living in a place like this,
right, Kankichi?

63
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,460
Soon you'll get to meet a real ninja!

64
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,680
I'm looking forward to it.

65
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:49,020
Being expected to do this much
makes me a little uneasy, though.

66
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,560
Well, whatever.

67
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:55,840
It does look like a ninja's house.

68
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,080
Yeah.

69
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:59,060
This place has quite a charm to it.

70
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:00,400
Stop it, Gepard.

71
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,300
What's wrong, Kankichi?

72
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:03,040
Listen, okay?

73
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,380
This is a ninja house, after all.

74
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,460
Just watch.

75
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:15,920
There's a trap set up to stop
intruders from the living room!

76
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:18,540
Don't set up such a dangerous trap.

77
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,160
Ow

78
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:24,280
One wrong step and Lemon
could have been badly hurt!

79
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,820
I didn't set it up.

80
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,280
Kankichi,
how are we supposed to get into the mansion?

81
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,680
Let me see, I think...

82
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,840
Found it, found it!

83
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,360
Oof.

84
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:52,060
It's really authentic, isn't it.

85
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:55,300
Is old man Koganemaruta in?

86
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,240
Nobody's home?

87
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,780
Well, we did let him know we were coming.

88
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:02,320
Should we go in and wait?

89
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,520
So this is what it's like.

90
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:12,940
Hey, Kankichi, it's Shirikenger!

91
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:15,200
Well, it is a ninja house.

92
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:16,860
Amazing.

93
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,020
There he is after all.

94
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:22,060
Looks like he's asleep.

95
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,915
Even though a customer
has come all this way,

96
00:06:24,965 --> 00:06:27,640
he doesn't notice,
so he doesn't seem like much of a ninja.

97
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,600
Well, there's nothing we can do about it.

98
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,220
Right.

99
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,820
Oh no, no, no.

100
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:56,180
It should've only taken three minutes,
but it's already past two.

101
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,260
Isn't that Ryotsu?

102
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,560
What are you doing here?

103
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:02,160
What a coincidence.

104
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,200
This little kid wants to meet a ninja?

105
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,500
Lemon, nice to meet you.

106
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,280
Okay, sure.

107
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,280
Either eat or talk, pick one.

108
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:18,040
I thought it felt hard to talk.

109
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,880
What a cheeky-looking kid.

110
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,200
It's because I only watch period dramas.

111
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,460
That's why I ended up talking like this.

112
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:28,500
For someone your age to love period dramas,
that's quite impressive.

113
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:31,360
That's right,
shall we all try some ninja training?

114
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:34,280
Yeah! I want to become a Lemon ninja!

115
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:41,320
Lemon, that suits you well. You're cute!

116
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,220
Do you think so?

117
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,680
Depart, that sash looks weird.

118
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,200
Shut up! This is what I find comfortable.

119
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:49,780
Well, as long as it doesn't
get in the way of movement.

120
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,920
Why do I have to wear this kind of outfit!

121
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:58,180
That's the special kunoichi version.

122
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,820
Big ears for scouting out the enemy.

123
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:06,020
Chainmail to protect your body.

124
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,120
Try winking for me.

125
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,980
Effective, right?

126
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:12,480
Confusing the enemy with that look,
it's the very essence of a kunoichi!

127
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,180
I see.

128
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:15,980
It's not weird at all!

129
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,860
Aaaah!

130
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:22,560
Aaaah, amazing!
It's the Ninjutsu: Turning Point Technique!

131
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,740
You're pretty good at this, aren't you?

132
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:28,080
There's no way this old man
can use ninja arts like that!

133
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,960
It's just a costume

134
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:34,080
And the kick actually landed properly, too.

135
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:36,800
Looks like we'd better stop after all

136
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,160
Lord Kogane-maru is

137
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,700
sleeping over there.

138
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:50,760
He looks more like a
ninja than Kogane-maru does.

139
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,580
Master,

140
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:55,780
don't breathe heavily in my ear.

141
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:56,780
That's disgusting.

142
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,680
Master, I'm terribly sorry,

143
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:00,340
but after all these years of your kindness,

144
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,440
I wish to leave here today for good.

145
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:05,380
What, you're going away too?

146
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:26,760
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

147
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:27,380
What's that?

148
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,780
That's the Ninja Land.

149
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,580
Look at all those buses and cars coming!

150
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:51,060
It's more of a theme park, really.

151
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:55,020
Ever since that was built,
all the tourists have been taken over there.

152
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,160
and this situation has kept going on and on.

153
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:01,180
No wonder they all ran off.

154
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,840
At this rate, I'll

155
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,520
end up starving to death.

156
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,960
Ryo-something,
how do we get those customers over there

157
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,940
back over here? Isn't there a way?

158
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:10,240
How should I know that?

159
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,900
Getting involved with you
never leads to anything good.

160
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:13,940
Let's go, everyone.

161
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:15,860
Wait, Kankichi.

162
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,460
After seeing someone in trouble,

163
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:20,960
you're just going to leave
without doing anything?

164
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,940
Are you even a man?

165
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:23,020
But...

166
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,540
It's better not to get involved here.

167
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,220
Lemon, if it's Kōmon-sama,
we'll definitely save him!

168
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,480
That's only something from TV shows.

169
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,440
Even if everyone goes home,
Lemon will save this old man!

170
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:39,100
Lemon, as expected, Princess Lemon!

171
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:40,560
Princess Lemon?

172
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,220
Ninja art: Seven Transformations!

173
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,475
Whoa,

174
00:10:44,525 --> 00:10:47,600
Cute.

175
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,477
Princess Lemon,

176
00:10:48,527 --> 00:10:51,680
he'll protect the princess
with his life's blood!

177
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,820
Hey, you switched the subject!

178
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,900
Don't flatter the kid.

179
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:01,680
No way.

180
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,940
Another useless ninja trick

181
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,440
It's the Ninja Art of Head Swapping!

182
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,600
I'm annoyed that I fell for it a little.

183
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:14,420
Can't be helped.

184
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:16,980
Guess I'll go out on a limb for Lemon.

185
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:20,080
Stop it, that's creepy!

186
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,060
There are more people here
than at some shoddy theme park

187
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,980
Yeah, it's the real deal.

188
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:47,760
Never mind that.
Can't you do something about this disguise?

189
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:52,180
We're here on a reconnaissance mission, so if our identities get exposed, that's bad.
Just bear with it.

190
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:55,700
Besides,
we're the ones standing out even more!

191
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,580
Excuse me, may we take a photo with you?

192
00:11:58,580 --> 00:11:59,560
Me too.

193
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,480
Next, me.

194
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,700
It's packed everywhere you look.

195
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:08,520
No matter how you look at it,
your side has no chance of winning.

196
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,280
Don't say something so easily.

197
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,720
Can't be helped, it's the truth.

198
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:14,800
Kankichi!

199
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:19,280
Fine, I can't be helped.

200
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,820
Would you like a sandwich or some juice?

201
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,180
One, please.

202
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,040
Here you go.

203
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,760
Hey! Take this seriously!

204
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,300
This is exactly why men are like this.

205
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:38,600
Would you like some tea?

206
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:40,520
One ninja bento.

207
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,800
Hey, hey.

208
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,340
Just from looking at this much,

209
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:47,720
I can see there's no way this can
compete with a real ninja house.

210
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,760
Wow, the Sanada-style
Ninja Land is something else.

211
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,960
Isn't there some way we can handle this?

212
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,920
Ryo-tsu, Hime!

213
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,560
You're...

214
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,300
Kankichi Ryotsu!

215
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:14,120
Who's this flashy woman?

216
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:17,740
Last spring at Spe, when we searched
for the Tokugawa hidden treasure,

217
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:21,300
the descendant of Sanada
Yukimura who tried to snatch it,

218
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,380
is the female thief boss.

219
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,320
Hand over the treasure!

220
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:35,440
This woman's the owner of Ninja Land? What?

221
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:41,540
I can't believe you know the old man
at that lame ninja house next door.

222
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,960
Shut up!
What are you doing in a place like this?

223
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:49,000
Weren't you arrested with
your gang and sent to prison?

224
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:52,060
I'm a ninja, if I put my mind to it.

225
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,500
Mumble, mumble, mumble.

226
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:59,600
Yeah, sorry it's a cheap,
lame, rundown ninja house!

227
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,860
I didn't say that much.

228
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:05,340
Whatever. I'm busy, so I'm leaving.

229
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,280
I've got to earn money for the best.

230
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,360
Bring it on, Meitsune.

231
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:12,900
Now that I know you're the boss here,

232
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,800
I'm suddenly motivated!

233
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,300
That's the spirit, Ryotsu!

234
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,380
Listen, I challenge you!

235
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:19,640
Challenge?

236
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:20,960
Challenge?

237
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,660
My Saigo-style ninjas and

238
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:26,440
your Sanada-style ninjas,
which are stronger?

239
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,860
Let's hold a ninja showdown.

240
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:30,540
Interesting.

241
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:31,780
I accept.

242
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,980
If we win,

243
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:39,160
we'll tear down that eyesore of a ninja house immediately,
is that right?

244
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,380
Fine.

245
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:44,480
Then if we win,
you'll vacate this place immediately!

246
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:46,320
Very well, then.

247
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:49,820
Sanada-style ninjutsu can't
possibly lose to country ninjutsu.

248
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,560
So, when's the match?

249
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,700
Tomorrow at noon, right here.

250
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:55,660
Agreed.

251
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:59,600
Old man, you'd better start
packing for your move today.

252
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:01,040
Hahahaha!

253
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,800
Old man, are you sure it's wise
to make a promise like that?

254
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:08,520
Yeah, a ninjutsu showdown...
you're not serious, are you?

255
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,430
Please, if it's a proper ninja,

256
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,460
when it comes to ninjutsu,
it's a fifty-fifty match.

257
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,100
Come on!

258
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:17,680
After all, with underhanded tactics,
nobody can beat us, you know.

259
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:18,860
Hahahaha!

260
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,340
That's the spirit!

261
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:23,980
Well, we're all human.
Win or lose, it can't be helped.

262
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,320
Alright, let's do this.

263
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,060
We're definitely going to win!

264
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,840
Why are the media here?

265
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,580
Kankichi, was this you?

266
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:42,820
I don't know.

267
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:43,840
Then who did?

268
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,220
I called the media.

269
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:55,740
It's a good chance to promote the
Sanada-style ninja and the Ninja Land.

270
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:58,940
That female ninja is quite capable,
isn't she.

271
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,780
Damn, Hōei-ken. So that was the trick.

272
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:08,260
A match is won by making the opponent say
"I give up" or by knocking them out.

273
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:11,320
Also, falling out of
the ring counts as a loss.

274
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:13,872
Kuno Hajime, to the two of them,

275
00:16:13,922 --> 00:16:16,920
these two are frail old men.
We have a chance to win.

276
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:20,340
No, even though they're decrepit old men,
those two

277
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:23,620
are descendants of Sarutobi
Sasuke and Kirigakure Saizō.

278
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,720
You'd better not underestimate them.

279
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:28,740
First ninja, to the center!

280
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,480
Just because she's a woman,
I won't go easy on you!

281
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:37,880
Bring it on!

282
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,700
Matoi! Do your best!

283
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:42,180
Fight!

284
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:45,820
Trained by Wan-chan,
take this naginata strike!

285
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:56,160
Chi-tan, you're pretty good, aren't you?

286
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:00,180
Now it's our turn to attack!

287
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:03,020
Big Choker Bomb!

288
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,500
Kabagaeru!

289
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,400
I'll do the keyboard.

290
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,980
No good! Endure it and somehow keep dodging!

291
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:19,280
Hang in there, Matoi!

292
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:19,820
No way...

293
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:22,540
Mama! No! Whoa!

294
00:17:23,060 --> 00:17:26,840
Hahaha, you stubborn girl,
I won't let you get away!

295
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:30,360
Sarare! Sarare!

296
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,140
Whoa! Ugh!

297
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,680
Matoi!

298
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,940
I can't take it anymore!

299
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,920
Come on, say you give up!

300
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,460
Hey! Lemon!

301
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:49,120
This is it! Matoi! Catch!

302
00:17:51,340 --> 00:18:13,120
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

303
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:15,220
Shanghai, the Saigo team wins!

304
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:18,920
Splendid, Matoi!

305
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,040
Now, the next match.

306
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,460
Kamako Yuri and Kankichi Ryotsu!

307
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:26,480
Leave it to you, Kamako.

308
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:27,400
Yes!

309
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,100
Right, my turn!

310
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:31,660
That's wrong! It's Saigo and Kanemaru!

311
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:33,860
Is that all right? Changing it on your own.

312
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:36,780
I see. Understood. Go ahead.

313
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:40,980
Is that really okay? Hold on!
You're the commander, aren't you?

314
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:44,940
We should win against an opponent we can
definitely beat here and take the upper hand.

315
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:48,340
Geez, you old lecher,
thinking the opponent is a woman!

316
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,680
One of the Sanada family,
Shigeo's descendants.

317
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:55,820
I'm Yurikama Koko, the
great-great-great-great-great-great-granddaughter of Yurikama Nosuke.

318
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:57,880
Now then, let us settle this fairly!

319
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,120
Come on, attack me from anywhere!

320
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,060
Ninjutsu!

321
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:04,840
Take this, you tooth-grinder!

322
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,860
Aaaaaah!

323
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:20,220
I give up.

324
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,920
He's a hopeless old pervert.

325
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,380
No choice, I'll go next.

326
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:27,180
Grandma, I'm counting on you.

327
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:43,780
Without a naginata,
you won't be able to lay a hand on us.

328
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:47,360
Granny, now's the time to use that ninpo!

329
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,740
Matoi, Kankichi!

330
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,100
W-what's the meaning of this?

331
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:57,100
I'll treat you to some
of that super Kanda sushi.

332
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,360
What's your favorite topping, pal?

333
00:19:59,360 --> 00:19:59,940
T-tuna belly.

334
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:00,620
Coming right up.

335
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,200
Here you go, thanks for waiting.

336
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:06,880
Delicious! Next, octopus and gizzard shad.

337
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:07,840
Coming right up.

338
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:08,820
Here you go.

339
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,300
Sea urchin and salmon roe!

340
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:16,420
Tengu, me, yellowtail and squid!

341
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,320
One more!

342
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:19,680
Free wasabi!

343
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,260
Gotcha!

344
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,840
The wasabi!

345
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,740
Water! Water! Water!

346
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:34,380
Sarutobi Sasukebe-san is out of bounds,
so the last team wins!

347
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,340
We did it! Granny!

348
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:38,280
Ninja art: sushi eating, isn't it?

349
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:40,660
Whew, every last one of them!

350
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:44,980
We can't lose now.
This fight's going to be a breeze.

351
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:49,120
We can't give up on the ninja park,
not when it's this popular.

352
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:51,680
We'll win at all costs
and steer it to a draw.

353
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:53,660
Strongest!

354
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:55,940
There!

355
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:01,960
Too bad

356
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:06,380
Don't let looks fool you. I'm one of the top
swordsmen in the entire Metropolitan Police Department.

357
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,300
Even without swords, we've got ninjutsu.

358
00:21:12,260 --> 00:21:14,340
Whoa, that's a perfect score!

359
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:15,860
Impossible.

360
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:16,540
Now!

361
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,440
Kankichi, watch out!

362
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:21,340
That was close.

363
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:23,060
Pulling dirty tricks like that, you bastard!

364
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:24,560
Where's the ninjutsu in that?

365
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,860
Ninjutsu: Killing Shadow Clone!

366
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:29,680
Whoa, our perfect score!

367
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,620
Damn it, you tricked us!

368
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,120
We didn't trick anyone.

369
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:36,040
I told you, it's a shadow clone technique.

370
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:37,720
There's a real one in there too.

371
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:39,680
What? Where? Where is it?

372
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:41,480
How about this?

373
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,540
Ninjutsu: Shadow Clone technique!

374
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:54,640
W-what?
Now we can't tell which one is the real one!

375
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,840
Kankichi! Look for the shadow!
The one with a shadow is the real one!

376
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:58,600
Shadow?

377
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:01,840
That one!

378
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,720
The real one!

379
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:09,420
That one's the real one too!

380
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:11,860
That's not what I meant!

381
00:22:11,860 --> 00:22:14,095
That one, that one, that one,

382
00:22:14,145 --> 00:22:16,240
that one, that one, that one.

383
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:19,840
What a splendid shadow clone technique.
Which one is the real one?

384
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,780
Looks like the match is over.

385
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:29,800
Appearing on TV was your mistake.

386
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:33,700
Haruka Sanada and your henchmen, you're
under arrest on suspicion of prison escape.

387
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:38,340
Prison escape? Haruka, you...

388
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:48,600
Hey, where the hell did those bastards go?

389
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,080
Over there!

390
00:22:53,520 --> 00:22:54,700
Too bad

391
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,040
Farewell!

392
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,800
Those guys...

393
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,680
Ryotsu, use this!

394
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,260
Yeah.

395
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:07,040
Stop it!

396
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:09,920
We did it!

397
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:10,920
We did it!

398
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:11,580
We did it!

399
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:12,420
We did it!

400
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:13,920
We did it!

401
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,060
We did it!

402
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,260
We did it!

403
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,220
We did it!

404
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,640
My mansion!

405
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:29,900
Aaaaaaah!

406
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:31,700
Aaaaaaah!

407
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,040
We finally won, and yet...

408
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,760
Now we've lost everything, haven't we.

409
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:44,180
See! Make him pay for it! Ryotsu!

410
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:47,200
You handed over the bow and arrows!
It's your fault!

411
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:51,300
Didn't I tell you not to
destroy the whole mansion too!

412
00:23:51,700 --> 00:23:52,880
See!

413
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:56,734
But...

414
00:23:56,784 --> 00:24:00,220
Now my summer diary is totally set!

415
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,440
Woo-hoo!

416
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,340
It's not in California, you know.

417
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:39,000
This isn't America, you know.

418
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,520
Sorry, Sori.

419
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:44,500
Uh, excuse me.

420
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:46,280
Yes, welcome!

421
00:24:47,340 --> 00:24:49,820
Then, kushiage, kakiage, and katsuage.

422
00:24:49,820 --> 00:24:51,680
Wait, everything here is fried, right?

423
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:53,660
What do you recommend?

424
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:56,960
Just watch out for the katsuage.

425
00:24:58,180 --> 00:25:00,740
Wait, are you related to him?

426
00:25:00,740 --> 00:25:02,420
Yeah, sorry about that, Sori.

427
00:25:03,820 --> 00:25:28,180
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

428
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:30,760
Whoa, you startled me.

429
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:35,220
I didn't recognize you at first. It's Mr. Omagari,
our homeroom teacher from elementary school!

430
00:25:35,220 --> 00:25:36,380
You're still alive?

431
00:25:36,380 --> 00:25:39,540
Decades have passed,
and you haven't changed a bit.

432
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:43,300
He says his youthfulness
comes from being in love.

433
00:25:43,780 --> 00:25:47,520
Next time:
"The Wacky Old Geezer Teacher." See you then!

434
00:25:51,780 --> 00:25:53,960
Surely in Kameari...

435
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:59,260
Everyone, come visit our town!

436
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

